#!/usr/bin/env python3

"""
AUDITOR DAILY CALL SAMPLING
===========================

Run:
    python auditor_sampling.py

No date argument is required.

The program automatically uses today's system date.

INPUT FILES
-----------

1. agent_auditor_mapping.csv

    auditor_id,agent_id


2. auditor_working_days.csv

    auditor_id
    month
    category
    required_calls
    working_days
    min_call_length
    max_call_length
    weekly_rule_within_category
    same_day_rule_across_category
    same_day_within_category
    vacation_date
    vacation_start_date
    vacation_end_date


3. daily_calls.csv

    call_id
    agent_id
    call_date
    run_date
    category
    call_length


OUTPUT
------

One Excel workbook per month:

    output/audit_sampling_YYYY-MM.xlsx


Excel sheets:

    Selections
        Permanent month-to-date selection history.

    Daily_Output
        All daily selections appended into one sheet.

    Run_Anchor
        First run date for the month.

    Audit_Stats
        Current monthly completion status.


IMPORTANT WEEK RULE
-------------------

Sampling weeks NEVER cross a calendar month.

Example:

Anchor:
    2026-08-03

August:

    Week 1 = Aug 03 - Aug 09
    Week 2 = Aug 10 - Aug 16
    Week 3 = Aug 17 - Aug 23
    Week 4 = Aug 24 - Aug 30
    Week 5 = Aug 31 only

September starts a new month and therefore
a new Week 1.

No August Week 5 can contain September dates.


RERUN BEHAVIOR
--------------

If today's job has already been run:

    1. Remove today's previous selections.
    2. Keep all previous days.
    3. Recalculate today's selections.
    4. Save today's new selections.

This makes the process safe to rerun.


VACATION
--------

Vacation dates do NOT prevent selection.

They are used to influence pacing.

Example:

    working_days = 21

    vacation_start_date = 2026-08-18
    vacation_end_date   = 2026-08-21

The program understands that the auditor has
less practical time toward the end of the month
and therefore increases pacing pressure before
the vacation period.

If no vacation is entered, normal Monday-Saturday
pacing is used.


CONSTRAINTS
-----------

weekly_rule_within_category
    Prevents multiple selections for the same
    auditor + agent + category within the same
    sampling week.

same_day_rule_across_category
    Prevents bind and policy change selections
    for the same agent on the same calendar day.

same_day_within_category
    Prevents multiple selections for the same
    agent + category on the same calendar day.


RELAXATION LADDER
-----------------

LEVEL 0:
    All configured constraints.

LEVEL 1:
    Relax weekly_rule_within_category.

LEVEL 2:
    Relax same_day_rule_across_category.

LEVEL 3:
    Relax same_day_within_category.

LEVEL 4:
    Relax call-length threshold.

The level is stored with every selection.


PACING
------

Pacing and constraint relaxation are separate.

Pacing determines whether the pair is due
for another selection.

Relaxation only happens when the quota is
genuinely at risk.

The program therefore does not immediately
relax constraints simply because today's call
does not fit.


CALL LENGTH
-----------

Normal selection:

    min_call_length <= call_length <= max_call_length

Among qualifying calls, the shortest call is selected.

At LEVEL 4, the length threshold is relaxed.
The call requiring the smallest movement outside
the configured range is selected.

"""

